ir value of $129, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 70%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $66.41 to $265 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 11.3 vs 18.7, EV/EBITDA 7.4 vs 11.0 and P/FCF 5.9 vs 16.5 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 17% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an FCF yield of 16.8% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 13.0% (vs the 8% bar).","The 2 covering analysts target $87.00 on average, 28% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 8% falls short of the cost of capital of 9.0%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.52).","It runs a 22% gross margin and converts 10% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.56x.","ROE of 25% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.9x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 7pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.6% of revenue on R&D and 1.0% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $16.7M (6% of market cap).","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 5.4, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.09)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.3% over 3 years, -0.8% over 5 years and -0.9% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 14%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 76%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.0x, 0.9% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 9, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 29.1% on average."],"own":["Insiders own 9.6%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 81%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (54 sales, net $2.9M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.5% (1.5% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 8.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 39 consecutive years, raising it 10.8% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 1,200 employees, each generates about $383K of revenue, in line with the Consumer Cyclical median.","That works out to $40K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.6M (4x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"score":47.2,"head":"Trades 47% below fair value of $129; against that, ROIC 8.1% vs WACC 9.0%.","pros":["Composite 47, above the 39 line (gates 13/25)","Trades 47% below fair value of $129","FCF margin 10.4%","Net cash of $16.7M","Piotroski F-score 7/9"],"cons":["ROIC 8.1% vs WACC 9.0%","Revenue shrank 0.8%/yr over 5y","Heavy insider selling ($2.9M net over 12 months)"],"flags":[],"vc":{"base":128.73,"base_src":"dcf","bear":66.41,"bull":265.23,"alt_median":25.61,"n_alt":3,"gap":4.0262,"dispersion":0.6972,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (70% dispersion)","DCF is 403% above the other models' median ($25.61)"]},"med":{"pe":18.6799,"ev_ebitda":11.018,"pfcf":16.4777,"pb":2.2768,"roic":0.1253,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0226}},"mc_quantiles":[38.77,54.81,66.41,75.66,82.62,90.67,98.83,105.98,114.47,123.32,132.22,141.98,151.91,162.34,175.92,190.04,209.26,233.46,265.23,317.63,459.54],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.656,"discount_rate":0.048,"terminal_growth":0.003,"exit_multiple":0.006,"base_fcf":0.287},"ticker":"FLXS","date":"2026-11-27"}